  "id": "systematic-sampling",
  "term": "systematic sampling",
  "definition": "Systematic sampling is a simple, commonly used way to choose a random sample from a finite population by following a fixed selection pattern. Variants of this approach, such as diagonal systematic sampling, are designed to improve precision in some situations, including when the population shows a linear trend.",
